Installing QCA
--------------

For Unix/Linux/Mac/Windows:

  cmake .
  make
  make install
  /sbin/ldconfig, if necessary

Notes
-----

  Use cmake cache entries

  CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX - must be defined otherwise QCA will be installed
                         in Qt prefix (by default: "")
  BUILD_TESTS - build unittests (by default: ON, OFF on Android)
  BUILD_TOOLS - build mozcerts and qcatool (by default: ON, OFF on Android)
  QCA_SUFFIX - suffix used together with the QCA ABI major version for the
               library, tools, headers, CMake package and pkg-config file
               (by default: "qt6" for Qt 6 and "qt5" for Qt 5)
  LIB_SUFFIX - library directory suffix (by default: "")
  LIB_INSTALL_DIR - path to library directory
                    (by default: ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib${LIB_SUFFIX})
  BUILD_PLUGINS - list plugins to build (botan;ossl;gnupg for example).
                  Also possible values is none, auto or all
                  (by default: "auto", "ossl" on Android)
  WITH_${PLUGIN}_PLUGIN - to build particular plugin. Can be no, yes or
                          auto (WITH_ossl_PLUGIN=auto for example)
  DEVELOPER_MODE - mode to enable features for developers. If ON
                   will be used hardcoded path to 'crypto'
                   (by default: OFF)
  OSX_FRAMEWORK - build an OS X framework (by default: ON)
  USE_RELATIVE_PATHS - make relocatable package if possible (by default: OFF)

  QCA 3 uses ABI-major-qualified install names so it can be installed next to
  QCA 2. With Qt 6 and the default suffix this includes:

    libqca3-qt6
    qcatool3-qt6
    mozcerts3-qt6
    Qca3-qt6/QtCrypto
    Qca3-qt6Config.cmake
    qca3-qt6.pc
    qca3-qt6/crypto

  CMake consumers should select the ABI explicitly:

    find_package(Qca3-qt6 CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(my_target PRIVATE Qca3::Qca)

  pkg-config consumers can use:

    pkg-config qca3-qt6

  Finally install paths can be overridden with:

  QCA_PREFIX_INSTALL_DIR - qca prefix, just a origin to make other paths
  QCA_PLUGINS_INSTALL_DIR - qca plugin root; providers are in its crypto subdir
  QCA_BINARY_INSTALL_DIR - qcatool and mozcerts will be installed to
  QCA_LIBRARY_INSTALL_DIR - qca library will be installed to
  QCA_FEATURE_INSTALL_DIR - path to qt mkspecs dir
  QCA_DATA_INSTALL_DIR - qca data and fallback certificate bundle
  QCA_INCLUDE_INSTALL_DIR - path for QtCrypto dir with includes
  QCA_PRIVATE_INCLUDE_INSTALL_DIR - for future implementation
  QCA_DOC_INSTALL_DIR - for html documentation
  QCA_MAN_INSTALL_DIR - for qcatool manpage
  PKGCONFIG_INSTALL_PREFIX - path to install pkg config file

Android
-------

  Android builds use the platform TrustManagerFactory as the QCA system
  certificate store. The accepted issuer certificates are imported into QCA
  directly in DER form; no CA bundle is copied from the build host and no Qt
  resource file is required.

  The Android defaults keep cross-builds minimal:

    BUILD_TESTS=OFF
    BUILD_TOOLS=OFF
    BUILD_PLUGINS=ossl

  All of these cache entries can still be overridden explicitly with -D.

Please report problems to:
  https://github.com/psi-im/qca/issues

Official fork repository:
  https://github.com/psi-im/qca
